# The whole shared tree is the Docker build context, because method
# Dockerfiles reference `methods/<name>/...` relative to its root. Docker tars
# the entire context before running the first instruction, so without this file
# every `graflag run --build` moved several GB to deliver a few KB.
#
# Measured on a populated checkout: .git 3.0 GB + datasets 3.0 GB, against
# 12-36 KB actually needed by a method build.
#
# Datasets are bind-mounted into the container at run time, never built in, and
# experiments are outputs. Neither belongs in a build context.

.git/
.github/
datasets/
experiments/

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Keep methods/ and libs/: Dockerfiles COPY from methods/<name>/, and the
# evaluator image is built from libs/graflag_evaluator/.
